            <abstract lang="en">
                <p>Various exemplary drug delivery devices with propellant, drug products utilizing the same, and methods of using drug delivery devices with propellant are provided. In general, a nasal drug delivery device is configured to expel a drug into a nose of a patient and to drive delivery of the drug using a propellant. The propellant includes a gas, e.g., air, carbon dioxide, etc., and/or at least one material substance configured to produce energy that causes movement of the drug out of an opening of the drug delivery device.</p>
            </abstract>
